 "flag": "q_arc_ni_2",
 "text": [
  "A display of the yard's records. Harland and Wolff began in 1861 on Queen's Island, and Titanic was launched on 31 May 1911.",
  "She carried about three million rivets, driven in squads of five: a heater boy, a catcher, a holder-up and two riveters hammering in turn. Only the ship's name is on the plaque. The squads' are in the ledgers.",
  "Someone has pencilled in the margin: 'Ask Mervyn Hanna.' It is in a very tidy hand."
 ]
